{"id": 64, "ts": 1780444164.2786584, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 4, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate the panel\u2019s leaning toward Candidate\u202fC, especially given the quick, correct decisions and strong attention skills noted. However, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fD is the safer overall choice for a long\u2011distance pilot. D demonstrates a solid blend of operational reliability and technical competence:\u202fhe responds adequately to unexpected events, concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, and takes responsibility seriously\u2014each a core requirement for high\u2011risk international flights. By contrast, Candidate\u202fC\u2019s difficulty communicating ideas, reputation as egocentric, and lack of willingness to pursue further education raise serious concerns about crew cooperation, professional communication, and adaptability, all of which are critical for sustained long\u2011haul operations. While D is described as moody and a loner, these traits are less directly tied to safety\u2011critical performance than the communication and learning gaps evident in C. Therefore, I continue to recommend Candidate\u202fD as the best fit for the position."}
