{"id": 79, "ts": 1780444229.6289752, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s clarification that Candidate\u202fC scores highly on reliability, rapid decision\u2011making and crew atmosphere, but I remain uneasy about the communication and egocentric concerns she raised. Those issues could undermine safety on long\u2011haul flights where clear, concise exchanges are vital. Moreover, Emily confirmed we have no concrete evidence of Candidate\u202fD\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation, yet we do know D is \u201cconsidered moody,\u201d which raises a red flag for temper management under stress. Given that D\u2019s strong points (problem\u2011solving, responsibility, concentration) are offset by an unverified but potentially serious temper issue, I am not convinced D outweighs C\u2019s proven reliability and decision quality. Therefore, I keep my provisional vote for **Candidate\u202fC**, while urging us to probe further into D\u2019s temperament and C\u2019s communication style before finalizing."}
