{"id": 83, "ts": 1780444251.5851488, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 5, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s support for Candidate\u202fD, especially his strong problem\u2011solving and responsibility. However, I\u2019m increasingly concerned about the crew\u2011cooperation risk his arrogance and weak leadership present on long\u2011haul flights. While Candidate\u202fC is 100\u202f% reliable and makes quick, correct decisions, his difficulty communicating ideas and egocentric attitude could jeopardize cockpit coordination under stress. In contrast, Candidate\u202fA not only anticipates dangerous situations and sees complex connections\u2014critical for long\u2011distance operations\u2014but also demonstrates very good leadership and excellent spatial vision. His main drawbacks are occasional resistance to criticism and some disorganization, which are more readily addressable through targeted training than the fundamental communication barriers seen in C or the attitude issues in D. Therefore, I now recommend Candidate\u202fA as the best overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot role."}
